  "limitations": [
    "The checks use synthetic signed releases, deterministic keys, a synthetic transparency checkpoint, and in-process API routers. They do not install a real Wrangler, EdgeOne, or Deislet driver release and do not deploy to a real provider account.",
    "The demo's end-to-end run, which is what proved the three product regressions this change set fixes, ran on Linux only. It is not part of this archive verification.",
    "The compiler's tests did not run on Windows: that host carries no libclang, so a native dependency cannot build. ADR-018 supports the compiler on Windows, so this is a real gap in coverage, not a boundary. Installing LLVM on that host closes it.",
